 "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Colorado remains a Democratic-leaning state at the presidential level, carrying a six-point Democratic partisan lean and no Republican presidential win in two decades. The 2028 race is an open contest with the incumbent term-limited, and neither party has settled on a nominee. No general-election polls or expert ratings are available yet, so the outlook rests on the state's underlying lean.\n\nEarly signals point Democratic: matchup polling reported in August 2026 shows leading Democratic contenders ahead of the top Republican names, while a Republican straw poll shows a still-contested field. June's primaries produced progressive upsets in Colorado, leaving the Democratic ticket's shape uncertain. The forecast gives Democrats a six-point expected margin, with wide uncertainty until nominees and state polls emerge.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7597, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6966, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7137, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.701, "margin": 6.0}]}